data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Write the centred data as $\\tilde X = U S V^\\top$. The rows of $V^\\top$ are the axes. The explained variance\nof axis $i$ is $s_i^2/(n-1)$, where $s_i$ is its singular value. The ratio divides by the total variance of\nall $d$ columns, not by the variance of the kept axes. Each kept axis then needs a sign chosen by the rule\nin the contract. The scores are the centred data projected onto the signed axes."},"hints_note":null}

